From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:29:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: bound the fragment jobs of an attachment-less pass
 to its draws

vkd3d-proton gives a pass without RTV and DSV a render area of
maxFramebufferWidth x maxFramebufferHeight and maxFramebufferLayers layers:
65536 x 65536 x 256 here. Since such passes no longer lose the device, they
take 2.9 s of GPU time each, with five 3-vertex draws into a 1x100
viewport (drawcpu noatt): a fragment job walks every tile of its bounding
box, 12 ms per layer at 65536x65536, although no tile outside the draws'
scissor boxes gets a fragment.

A pass with no attachment loads and stores nothing, so the side effects of
its fragments are all it does, and fragments only exist inside the box a
draw is rasterized with. Track the union of those boxes from the dynamic
state at each draw: the scissor, intersected with the viewport before v12
(the SCISSOR_BOX register holds their intersection there), rounded
outwards, and use it, clamped to the render area, as the fragment jobs'
bounding box. Draws whose prerast shader picks one of several viewports
(their box is the framebuffer), vk_meta rectangle draws and
vkCmdExecuteCommands stop the tracking: those passes keep the full render
area. A secondary continuing a render pass never tracks. Passes with an
attachment are unchanged.

drawcpu noatt at 65536x65536x256 goes from 2,910 ms to 8 ms (5 draws), and
to 1.1 s when the draws' boxes spread over 48000x36000; the atomic counts
are the same. Passes with attachments are unchanged (ircheck checksums
identical).

PANVK_NO_NOATT_FRAG_BBOX=1 restores the full render area.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
